da has  taken to date to successfully lead the  efp battle group in latvia and i will  say that stands as an example  which many countries themselves point to  as a way in which nato's eastern flank  has been effectively protected and will  continue to be effectively protected  with the collaboration and cooperation  that we will continue to utilize going  forward and i guess i will just add that  you know in response to your comment  what is taking so long i think  really to be fair we have to look at the  increases  even in recent months of canada's  commitment to the eastern flank and  latvia in particular  we've added  an artillery battery to the enhanced  ford presence battle group in latvia  we've added an electronic warfare troop  we've added a retast halifax class  frigate to nato standing naval forces  we've added a maritime patrol aircraft  two tactical airlift aircraft with air  detachment and headquarters staff to  support multinational division north as  my colleague just pointed out so we are  continuing to increase our commitment in  latvia and that's what today is all  about  re-committing to an additional new stage  of our relationship with latvia and our  leadership role in latvia
 

